The upstream MIT notice is preserved in LICENSES/gcs_python-MIT.txt.
The original Python geometry is based on the SolarSoft GCS routines and the
Thernisien graduated cylindrical shell model, as noted in geometry.py.

The historical proposal file was derived from the curated matched-event records
used by Singh et al. (2022), ApJ 933, 123, DOI: 10.3847/1538-4357/ac73f3.
Its provenance, source-workbook checksum, excluded events and angular conventions
are recorded in historical_gcs_proposals.json. The original workbooks are not
distributed here.

Example image data originate from STEREO/SECCHI COR2 (NRL), retrieved through
Helioviewer. The manifest records the source IDs, observation times and checksums.
Processed example maps are standardized pre-event image differences, with original
observer metadata. The software license does not claim ownership of third-party
solar observations; retain their scientific attribution when reusing them.
